Database migrations (Alembic).

The application does NOT create tables at startup. The schema is produced only
by the migrations here, so that every environment gets the same one.

New database
    alembic upgrade head

Database that predates Alembic (has tables, no alembic_version)
    alembic stamp head          # mark the baseline as applied, run nothing
    alembic upgrade head        # apply anything newer

    Running `upgrade` without stamping first fails with DuplicateTable, because
    the baseline migration tries to create tables that already exist.

Adding a migration
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "what changed"
    # read the generated file before committing — autogenerate misses things
    # like server defaults and it renders drops for anything it cannot see
    alembic upgrade head

Checking
    alembic current             # where this database stands
    alembic check               # does the schema match the entity definitions

Notes
    The database URL comes from src.container.settings via alembic/env.py, not
    from alembic.ini, so migrations and the app cannot point at different
    databases.

    db_types.UUID renders as sa.Uuid() in migrations (see render_item in
    env.py). Migrations must not import application code: they are a historical
    record and have to keep working after that code moves.

